{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2bf837fb238829ea","name":"Outlaw Tech","source":{"id":"source:reference-2bf837fb238829ea","title":"Outlaw Tech","revision":18989,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:05:42Z","sha256":"dfedd8326a288f1af72a38d1d60de341283726552d1b1561ad2db894d4db6e68","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18989","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Outlaw%20Tech&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2bf837fb238829ea","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Outlaw Tech combines technological know-how with criminal tendencies. They are an expert at breaking and entering, and are as comfortable hijacking a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," as they are hotwiring a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder"},". Their tools are some of their most valued possessions, and they range from high-end ",{"tag":"a","children":["Datapads"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Datapads"}," to specialized ",{"tag":"a","children":["Security Kits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Security_Kits"},". They pride themselves on getting the job done quickly, and approaches each new assignment with childlike zeal. They are an opportunist, but they're also willing to plan ahead when time allows them the luxury of doing so.  \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because they are both charismatic and intelligent, an Outlaw Tech is just as capable at gaining a mark's confidence as they are at hacking a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Code Cylinder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Code_Cylinder","referenceId":"reference:e8825fcee2d6d69f"},". This versatility allows the Outlaw Tech to be more flexible in the field, and to approach each new situation differently depending on the circumstances. They know how to do their homework, because they have friends on the street who can feed them the information they need. An Outlaw Tech also keeps up on the latest technology, even if they can't afford it, because they might someday come up against it in the course of their job. \n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Outlaw Tech Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Outlaw Techs are everywhere, plying their trade throughout the galaxy with varying degrees of success. They work on the wrong side of the law, and are often pitted against the authorities whether or not they succeed on their current job. Particularly gifted Outlaw Techs might find steady employment with criminal syndicates or less than savory corporate interests, but most work on a freelance basis. Some even work as legitimate technicians, using the information they gather during their normal work hours to develop new plans and schemes. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though capable in a fight, Outlaw Techs are not frontline combatants. They prefer to fight from a distance, using ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cover"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealment"}," as the snap off well-aimed shots from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"},". They're not above shooting someone in the back, especially if doing so will bring a quick end to a potentially messy firefight. Utilizing their skills to seal a blast door between themselves and their enemies is also perfectly acceptable. Hand-to-hand combat is never something that Outlaw Techs seek to engage in; they prefer to leave such activity to the soldiers and thugs who do it best. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Outlaw Tech Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 2/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +9; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", Durese, Sullustese\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 19 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 17), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 16, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 17\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 30, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 16\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 6 Squares\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unarmed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unarme